# Intent: the restart guard never leaves the unit frozen (owner 2026-11-16: a unit whose self-restarts were used up, "3 of 3", sat frozen). Patch R02 refused every restart after the third in an hour and asked for a stall restart only once per freeze, so a fourth freeze stayed a freeze until the hour ended or someone reset the unit by hand. Now the first three restarts in a window go at once; after that a restart is allowed once the unit has run 5, then 10, then 20, then at most 30 minutes since its last restart (maipai_heal_core.h, mhc_allow), and the stall watch asks again every minute for as long as the freeze lasts, so a held-back request is only a wait. A fault that returns at once is still held back, never into a reboot loop (at most one restart per 5 minutes at the fastest), and a freeze that returns after a long run is always cleared. The refusal log line and the heal event (action=refused) now carry wait_s and are sent at most every 5 minutes; one request is decided at a time. The boot event's heal_hold follows the same rule. New: on the first stall ask the motion task logs every task (name, state, priority, free stack) and sends one heal event (action=stall, t=main/lvgl/esp_timer/audio/ws states), so the next freeze names its cause instead of only being cleared (patch 069 of the older line did this and was dropped from the rebuild).
# Placement: unit (a basic the robot must do alone; it runs with the host off)
# Upstream: main/hal/maipai_heal.cc from patch R02 (MIT); new hal/maipai_heal_core.h (MIT)
# Check after a flash: three host reboot requests in a row restart the unit three times; the fourth within five minutes of the last logs "restart held back ... allowed in N s" once; a main loop held for 30 s while three restarts are already counted logs "main loop stalled" again every minute and restarts at the first minute the back-off allows.
